title = "For Developers"
template = "docs"
description = "Orientation for developers: build plugins and themes, automate Revela, or contribute to its code."
+++

As a developer, you can extend Revela with your own plugins and themes, script it in CI, or help build Revela itself. This page points you to the right place. Contributor documentation lives next to the code on GitHub, so it stays current with every change.

## Build on Revela

<div class="path-grid">
<a class="path-card" href="https://github.com/Spectara/Revela/blob/main/docs/plugin-development.md"><span class="path-title">🧩 Plugin Development <span class="arrow">→</span></span><span class="path-desc">Implement <code>IPlugin</code>, register services, add CLI commands, test and package your plugin.</span></a>
<a class="path-card" href="https://github.com/Spectara/Revela/tree/main/src/Sdk"><span class="path-title">📦 SDK <span class="arrow">→</span></span><span class="path-desc"><code>Spectara.Revela.Sdk</code>: the public interfaces for plugins and themes. The package is attached to every GitHub Release.</span></a>
<a class="path-card" href="theme-authoring/"><span class="path-title">🎨 Theme Authoring <span class="arrow">→</span></span><span class="path-desc">Build a theme or change one deeply with Scriban templates: required partials, image helpers, UI text and extensions.</span></a>
<a class="path-card" href="../reference/template-functions/"><span class="path-title">🧰 Template Functions <span class="arrow">→</span></span><span class="path-desc">Every function and variable available in templates.</span></a>
</div>

## Automate Revela

Every menu entry is also a command, so Revela runs unattended in scripts and CI pipelines. Start with the [CLI Reference](../reference/cli-reference/) and the [Configuration guide](../guide/configuration/) (settings can also come from environment variables). The [Deployment guide](../guide/deployment/) includes a GitHub Actions example.

